# Q: how much of each surface is on the map, and is there any lava at all?
#
# A surface with a movement cost, a cover value, a colour and a shader treatment can
# still be a surface no cell ever receives — that has happened twice here (sand, then
# lava). A screenshot cannot show a surface that is missing; a census shows it in one
# line, including the zeros.

surfaces

# The same question one cell at a time, with the height that decides it: a cell is water
# when its ground is below the water line, and this prints both numbers.
attributes 0 0
attributes -180 -180

# And what the camera can see of it, which is the other half of "why is the picture
# empty": the ground the frustum covers, and the surfaces absent from it.
visible

# The counts above are a ledger. Two of them are worth pinning: lava exists, and the
# map is not all one surface. These fail loudly if a terrain change takes either away.
expect "the map has lava" 55 55
expect "the map has woodland" 976 976
expect "the navigation lattice is 65 x 65" 4225 4225
